more legal trouble for Johnson &amp; Johnson  a philadelphia jury has ordered it to  pay 8 billion dollars in punitive  damages in a case unrelated to a string  of big money lawsuits over its signature  baby powder now the jury found the  company failed to warn a man taking the  anti-psychotic drug risperdal of its  side-effects our consumer investigative  reporter andrew warner has been  following the story and joins us at the  table and do you think it paves the way  for other lawsuits like this well that's  a big question right I mean there are  thousands of these lawsuits out there  what does this mean for them 8 billion  dollars is lot it was awarded in the  case of 26 year old Nicholas Marie who  said taking risperdal as a child caused  him to develop breasts an incurable  condition known as gynecomastia  thousands of others have filed lawsuits  alleging the same Murray said he was  prescribed the medicine at age 9 for  symptoms related to autism spectrum  disorder the FDA's approval of the drug  in the 1990s was to treat schizophrenia  and episodes of bipolar mania in adults  now attorneys for Murray alleged the  company marketed the drug for unapproved  off-label use in children to increase  profits choosing quote what they called  billions over children Johnson &amp; Johnson  denies the allegations and says it's  confident that this ruling will be  overturned in a statement the company  says it was quote precluded from  presenting key evidence which it says  showed how the label for the drug  clearly inappropriately outlined the  risks associated with the medicine I  spoke with Murray's attorneys last night  they told me the punitive damages were  meant to deter the company from similar  conduct in the future and they believe  the award will stand but of course eight  billion dollars we've seen a lot of  these big verdicts shut down by judges  later yeah that's a very big one that is  cut it down it's gonna be big gets your  attention there sends a message may not  you know we'll see what happens with it  alright Anna thank you very much
 

